# autotune: the CW fine-tuning assistant (issue #190, "Auto Tune v2") triggered
# from the real main screen and cancelled by a second press.
#
# The route is the user's: the APP key loads buttons_group_app (src/main_screen.c,
# KEYPAD_APP), the page button cycles to page 6 and the "Auto Tune" button
# (src/buttons.cpp, make_action_btn("Auto\nTune", ACTION_ATUNE)) is pressed, which
# reaches main_screen_action(ACTION_ATUNE) -> autotune_ui_toggle() -> the session
# starts in COLLECT.
#
# The radio is in CW, which is the only family Auto Tune works in. The bank has
# NO CW tone by default (mocks/mock_cw_tune.c starts with no signal): during
# COLLECT the dial does NOT move - v2 never sweeps, there is no probe zigzag and
# no progress bar - and a second press cancels the session. scenario_settle
# codifies all three facts: the session started, the dial stayed exactly at the
# fixture frequency while collecting, and the cancel left it there.
#
# The other fixtures of the family: `autotune-progress` (the single provisional
# correction, mid-session), `autotune-found` (the same correction verified) and
# `autotune-notcw` (the rejection outside CW/CWR). "Tuned" against real RF is the
# owner's radio: docs/autotune.md.

name autotune
screen autotune

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode cw
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
